@ 7 - Algonquian
# citation: Proto-Algonquian is believed to have had the following phonology, as provided for by the Wikipedia: The phoneme denoted as /θ/ may well have been actually /ɬ/ instead. Also, some debate exists as to whether or not /r/ was originally an /l/. (From Wikipedia contributors (2011), “Proto-Algonquian language”. Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia. <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Proto-Algonquian_language>)